 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Lines 286-299 of the file; Mathlib never encodes the derivative value in a `hasDerivAt_*` name (`hasDerivAt_exp`, `hasDerivAt_sinh`, `hasDerivAt_arctan`, `hasDerivAt_negMulLog` all name the function), and in this repo `hasDerivAt_neg_photonFluxProfile` (Flux/Basic.lean:154) likewise names the function, not the derivative.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/SpecialFunctions/BesselK/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Rename so the derivative description cannot occupy the order slot and names both terms, e.g. `hasDerivAt_besselK_eq_neg_besselK_sub_one_sub_div`; do not leave `_neg_besselK_sub_one` where `_zero`/`_one` mean the order.",
   "issue": "`hasDerivAt_besselK_neg_besselK_sub_one` states `K_\u03bd' = -K_{\u03bd-1} - (\u03bd/x) K_\u03bd`, but its suffix names only the first of the two derivative terms, and in the same file the suffix after `hasDerivAt_besselK` denotes the order (`hasDerivAt_besselK_zero` line 292 = order 0, `hasDerivAt_besselK_one` line 297 = order 1). The name therefore reads as `K\u208d\u208bK_{\u03bd-1}\u208e'` and advertises `K_\u03bd' = -K_{\u03bd-1}`, which is false.",
   "line": 286
  }
 ],
